    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1723">

                <pb facs="1102" n="986" xml:id="pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11D29/51.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Answering your April 7, at hand on my return from the trip to interior with
                    officials of Panama. I have not yet succeeded in communicating with Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs. It is doubtful whether it can be done before Monday on account
                    of Holy Week. I have been insistent and persistent in these matters. Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs just before trip above mentioned assured me progress in the
                    matter was real.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
